<title>THAILAND: Thai banks seen hurt if Moody's cuts ratings.</title>
<headline>Thai banks seen hurt if Moody's cuts ratings.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Thailand Governor Rerngchai Marakanond said on Tuesday local commercial banks will have higher funding costs and lower earnings if Moody's Investors Service cuts their credit ratings.</p>
<p>&quot;Moody's has not made any cut in the ratings of Thai banks yet. If the credit ratings were really downgraded banks' funding costs will rise and their earnings will be lower,&quot; Rerngchai told reporters.</p>
</text>
